<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28372" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕdon</span></b> , ontis,
		m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μέδων</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A Centaur</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
				303</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Son of Codrus, king of Athens, the first
			archon;</i> hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mĕdontĭdae</span></b> ,
			ārum, m., <i>his
				descendants</i>, <i><span class="en">Vell. 1, 2,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>One of Penelope's suitors; acc.</i> Medonta, Sabin.
			Ep. 1, 47.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
